# liburm1 intentionally ships all five URM shared libraries in a single binary
# package rather than one package per SONAME. The libraries
# (libContextualClassifier, libRestuneCore, libUrmAuxUtils, libUrmClient,
# libUrmExtAPIs) are built from one source tree, all carry SOVERSION 1, and are
# versioned and released in lockstep by upstream -- they are not independently
# consumable. Splitting them into five packages would add four binary packages
# with no practical gain for consumers, who always need the whole set.
#
# Should upstream ever bump one library's SOVERSION independently, this
# aggregation becomes wrong and the package must be split per SONAME, with the
# usual library transition.
liburm1: package-name-doesnt-match-sonames libContextualClassifier1 libRestuneCore1 libUrmAuxUtils1 libUrmClient1 libUrmExtAPIs1
# For C++ libraries, we're explicitly avoiding the .symbols file
liburm1: no-symbols-control-file
